# Terms that must never appear in the public tree, one per line, matched
# case-insensitively as extended regex alternatives by tools/make-public-tree.
#
# Copy this file to `.private-terms` (gitignored) and list your own. If no such file
# exists the check is skipped and the build says so — it is never silently weakened.
#
# WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE, IGNORED FILE. The list is personal in its own right: naming a
# former employer here discloses that employer to anyone who reads it. The first public
# push of this repo shipped five such terms on one line, in the very script whose job was
# to keep them out — the script was exempt from its own checks so it could hold them, and
# shipping the script shipped the list. The mechanism belongs in the repo; the terms do
# not.
#
# What belongs here: employers, your home town, clients, internal tools or vendors you
# used, anything that identifies your search rather than the toolkit. Keep each term
# broad enough to catch variants — "acme" rather than "Acme Corporation Ltd".
#
# What does NOT belong here: your own name. That has its own check (ALLOW_NAME), which
# deliberately exempts `backlog/` and `log/` — a byline in a signed design document is
# expected; a former employer in the roadmap is not.

# acme corp
# some city
# internal-tool-name
